01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
The Red Sea Diving Resort (also known as Operation Brothers) is a 2019
spy thriller film written and directed by Gideon Raff.

13
01:20:28,571 --> 01:20:34,571
The film stars Chris Evans as an Israeli Mossad agent who runs a covert operation to
rescue Ethiopian-Jewish refugees from Sudan to safe haven in Israel.

14
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
Williams, Haley Bennett, Alessandro Nivola, Michiel Huisman, Chris Chalk,
Greg Kinnear, and Ben Kingsley are in supporting roles.

15
01:32:51,428 --> 01:32:57,428
The film is loosely based on the events of Israel's Operation Moses and Operation Joshua in 1984-1985, in which the Mossad covertly rescued Jewish-Ethiopian refugees who suffered from persecutions in Sudan in
Africa, by smuggling them all the way to the safety of Israel, using a base at the once-abandoned holiday resort of Arous Village on the Sudanese Red Sea coast, about 70km (43 miles) north of Port Sudan.

16
01:39:02,857 --> 01:39:08,857
The Red Sea Diving Resort premiered at the San Francisco Jewish Film Festival on
July 28, 2019, and was released on July 31, 2019, by Netflix.

17
01:45:14,285 --> 01:45:20,285
Critical reaction to the film was predominantly negative,
while audiences were mixed to positive.

18
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The movie has been criticized for its white savior narrative.

19
01:57:37,142 --> 01:57:43,142
The film explores themes of israel, mossad, refugee camp, ethiopia, sudan.

20
02:03:48,571 --> 02:03:54,571
